  "notes": "Xiaomi TV EA Pro 55\" (MiTV-MTEQ0, codename baymax; sold as L55MA-EP), China-market firmware 23.6.26.4028,\nAndroid 10 (SDK 29, QQ2A.200305.004.A1), MediaTek/MStar, 3840x2160 panel (Android reports a 1080p UI mode).\nStock launcher: com.mitv.tvhome (HOME activity .MainActivityUserMode). Live TV / sources: com.xiaomi.mitv.tvplayer.\n\nApply:   TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/disable.sh examples/xiaomi-mitv-mteq0/debloat.txt\nUndo:    TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/restore.sh examples/xiaomi-mitv-mteq0/debloat.txt com.mitv.tvhome\nEverything is DISABLED, not uninstalled. Comment out any line you want to keep.\nUsed for a day with two reboots and several standby cycles; nothing broke that is not noted here.\n\nNotes from this firmware (details in docs/devices/xiaomi-mitv-mteq0-baymax.md):\n- Home: the framework only accepts system apps or allowlisted package names as HOME, like the\nMiTV-AETP0. The opt-in build -PlauncherApplicationId=com.ts.launcher (docs/devices/xiaomi-mitv-aetp0-dofus.md)\nwas accepted here: HOME resolved to it, also after a reboot and after a force-stop like the one\nstandby does. With the standard com.gathin.tvhome ID, disabling com.mitv.tvhome leaves\nFallbackHome (a black screen).\n- Network ADB closes at every boot: com.xiaomi.mitv.settings writes adb_enabled=0 a few seconds after\nboot. Re-enable it under Settings > Account & Security > ADB debugging.\n- Standby (power key) force-stops every non-system app after 2 s (MitvPowerManagerService ->\nkillAllThirdApp) unless a cloud allowlist exempts it. Android then drops any accessibility service\nof those apps, so do not rely on an accessibility helper on this set.\n- com.xiaomi.mitv.upgrade and com.mediatek.TimeMeasurementAgent are persistent: the firmware starts them\nat boot even when disabled. Disabling still blocks their components; the processes stay.\n- Shell cannot disable single components, `pm hide` (no MANAGE_USERS) or `pm uninstall --user 0`\n(DELETE_FAILED_INTERNAL_ERROR) on this firmware, so whole-package disables are the only tool.\n- Wi-Fi 5 GHz: the Wi-Fi country code comes from Settings.Global service_region and falls back to CN,\nwhich hides 5 GHz networks on channels 100-144. `settings put global service_region <CC>` and a Wi-Fi\noff/on fixes it.\n- Xiaomi's package installer has no CONFIRM_INSTALL screen: stores that install split APKs through a\nPackageInstaller session (Aptoide) hang at 80%. Stores using ACTION_VIEW (single APKs) work.\n- No Google services: the official YouTube TV app refuses to run; SmartTube works.\n- Privacy toggles worth flipping as well: settings put secure allow_oaid_used 0 (OAID ad ID),\nsettings put global individual_privacy_enabled 0 (personalised recommendations).\nXiaomi telemetry, diagnostics and log upload",
